\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2007\par 23:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Thursday as mining company shares gained sharply.   \par \par \uc2 A strong showing by  \uc2 Telefonica SA\uc2  (TEF), which is listed on the Lima Stock Exchange, also helped lift the overall indexes.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 225.59 points, or 1.02%, to end at 22,402.72.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 523.47 points, or 1.36%, to finish at 39,075.32.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rose 1.0% to end at $136.85, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) gained 1.7% to $30.10.   \par \par \uc2 Miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) advanced 2.4% to 155.95 soles ($51.81).   \par \par \uc2 Telefonica SA\uc2  rose 8.3% to end at $87.75, following the direction of its New York-traded American Depositary Receipt.   \par \par \uc2 Spain's Telefonica said Thursday that it will bring forward plans to raise its dividend payout and that it is aiming to boost earnings per share by more than 75% by 2010.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $181 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions, aiming to smooth movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The sol weakened slightly Thursday, ending at a midrate of PEN3.0165 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.016-PEN3.017.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.0155 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.015-PEN3.016.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 10-11-07 1700ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020071011e3ab000t3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
