\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2007\par 22:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Tuesday, given a lift by stronger mineral prices and by strength on Wall Street.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 122.73 points, or 0.56%, to end at 22,034.66.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index gained 229.77 points, or 0.61%, to finish at 38,204.95.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rose 2.4% to end at $128.50 on improved copper prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 0.2% to $29.15.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) rose 1.5% to $70.25.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $53 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions, aiming to smooth out movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol has continued to strengthen.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended Tuesday at a midrate of PEN3.0190 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.0180 to PEN3.0200.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.0200 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.0190 to PEN3.0210.   \par \par \uc2 Peru's sol could end 2007 at stronger than the psychologically important level of 3.00 to the U.S. dollar, Scotiabank said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 The bank, which forecasts the sol will appreciate 4.4% in 2007 and 5.8% in 2008, says the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to a number of factors.   \par \par \uc2 Among these are a strong trade surplus, a large surplus in the financial account, the international weakness of the dollar and an improvement in the nation's credit risk.   \par \par \uc2 It also points to ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars, and efforts by the government to replace the use of the dollar in the economy with the sol.   \par \par \uc2 In a separate report, financial consulting firm Macroconsult said that "It would be expected that the (appreciating) trend will continue until next year, as it would be difficult for it to be reverted."   \par \par \uc2 It pointed to, among other factors, tighter monetary policy in Peru and inflows of funds for investments.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 10-09-07 1630ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020071009e3a900080\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
