\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2007\par 22:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended lower Friday as various mining companies declined on weaker mineral prices.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 118.55 points, or 0.54%, to end at 21,822.99.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index decreased 281.52 points, or 0.74%, to finish at 37,710.49.   \par \par \uc2 Weaker prices for the red metal dragged down two key miners that had posted strong recent gains.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) fell 0.6% to end at $124.50, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) decreased 3.3% at end at $28.83.   \par \par \uc2 Lower tin prices dragged down Peru's only tin miner. Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) fell 1.0% to end at 10.35 soles ($3.38).   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $60 million.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol continued to strengthen.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended at a midrate of PEN3.0625 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.0400 to PEN3.0850, the official said.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of 3.0960 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.0950 to PEN3.0970.   \par \par \uc2 "There are large quantities of dollars that are entering from the strong exports, remittances and investments. It is like any other product; when there is an excess the price drops," Javier Kapsoli, the finance minister's director of economic and social affairs, told reporters.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that to September 26 the sol appreciated 1.8% from the end of August.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 09-28-07 1630ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070928e39s000s9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
