\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Weakens A Bit   \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2007\par 22:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes rose on Monday, boosted by rising metals prices that lifted mining company shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 238.06 points, or 1.13%, to end at 21,352.51.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 488.94 points, or 1.34%, to finish at 37,005.77.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) increased 2.9% to $123.50, on higher copper prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 1.7% to end at $27.25.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) gained 2.6% to end at 13.13 soles ($4.22) as zinc prices improved.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly weaker Monday at a midrate of PEN3.1145 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1140 to PEN3.1150.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1135 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1130 to PEN3.1140.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, following heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase dollars last week.   \par \par \uc2 The sol gained last week in part due to demand from local companies, mainly exporters, for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for monthly tax payments.   \par \par \uc2 Consulting company Macroconsult said in a report that demand for the sol has also come from local and foreign investment funds.   \par \par \uc2 The maturing of U.S. dollar forward contracts last week also increased demand for the sol.   \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said that no non-delivery forward contracts matured on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 To Sept. 19 the sol had appreciated 1.1% from the end of August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 09-24-07 1638ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070924e39o000g2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
