\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2007\par 22:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Friday after the U.S. Senate Finance Committee gave its approval to a free trade agreement with Peru.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index gained 351.65 points, or 1.69%, to end at 21,114.45.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 636.78 points, or 1.77%, higher at 36,516.83.   \par \par \uc2 "The free trade agreement is looking increasingly likely," one trader said. "Investors are encouraged."   \par \par \uc2 The free trade deal between Peru and the U.S. was approved by Peru's Congress in June 2006 but still awaits approval by the U.S. Congress.   \par \par \uc2 Agricultural producer Empresa Agroindustrial Pomalca SAA (POMALCC1.VL) gained 4.8% to 1.09 soles ($0.35).   \par \par \uc2 Sugar producer Empresa Agroindustrial Casa Grande SAA (CASAGRC1.VL) gained 3.1% to PEN13.67.   \par \par \uc2 Stronger copper prices also boosted investor confidence Friday, the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 2.6% to end at $26.80.  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) gained 1.8% to $120.00.   \par \par \uc2 Unionized workers at Southern Copper's Cuajone mine and Ilo smelter and refinery in Peru voted Thursday to strike on Oct. 2, union leaders said. Workers at the Toquepala mine had voted for the Oct. 2 strike on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended at a midrate of 3.1135 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1130 to PEN3.1140.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1190 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1180 to PEN3.1200.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $181 million, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 09-21-07 1645ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070921e39l000jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
