\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Strengthens Again   \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2007\par 22:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes fell Thursday as investors took profits after days of sharp gains.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 237.00 points, or 1.13%, to end at 20,762.80.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index lost 511.83 points, or 1.41%, to finish at 35,880.05.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) fell 0.7% to end at $26.11, after rising 5.6% Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) lost ground, easing 1.8% to end at 147.70 soles ($47.29). The share had gained 8.2% the day before.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP), which owns Peru's largest bank, also declined, ending 0.7% lower at $65.00. It had gained 4.9% on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) increased 2.5% to $117.90 on higher copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $50 million.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol ended stronger, at a midrate of PEN3.1119 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1118 to PEN3.1200.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1235 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1230 to PEN3.1240.   \par \par \uc2 The sol has gained in recent days in part due to demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for monthly tax payments, and on strong demand for soles from foreign investors.   \par \par \uc2 Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $135.5 million after buying $115 million on Tuesday, aiming to smooth out volatility and build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 "Dollar inflows into the country are high, despite the recent global turmoil; thus, we do not expect a change in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the near term,"  \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 "We think that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating significantly," it said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 09-20-07 1639ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070920e39k000fl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
