\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Stronger; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2007\par 22:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended slightly higher Monday as investor jitters eased.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the general index gained 66.66 points, or 0.30%, to end at 22,283.74.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended up 131.84 points, or 0.33% higher, at 39,546.68.   \par \par \uc2 "Stock markets around the world were stronger today. The waters have calmed. The markets, however, are extremely volatile right now," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 "The local market reacts to that volatility, but Peru is also cushioned by its excellent economic performance," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Stronger copper prices helped boost  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) shares 4.7% to $101.30.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner  \uc2 Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SA\uc2  (CVERDEC1.VL) also gained, rising 0.6% to end at $26.75.   \par \par \uc2 Blue chip financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) gained 0.8% to end at $62.50.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended stronger at a midrate of 3.1470 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1460 to PEN3.1480.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1495 on a spread of PEN3.1490 to PEN3.1500.   \par \par \uc2 "The national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in demand for monthly tax payments," one analyst said.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $65 million, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly this year to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com; [ 13-08-07 2059GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020070813e38d0003o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
