\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2007\par 22:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended lower Friday as weaker metal prices and a decline in shares on Wall Street pulled down the local market.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 93.34 points, or 0.41%, to end at 22,950.22.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 126.60 points, or 0.31%, lower at 40,926.20.   \par \par \uc2 "Overall the Peruvian market is very strong, but it is always influenced by outside markets. The drop the market took this week is the effect of the hard hit the North American markets are taking," said Edwin Paz, a trader with brokerage Provalor.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) declined 4.7% to end at $102.00, as copper prices weakened.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 0.9% to end at 16.42 soles ($5.20) as zinc prices eased.   \par \par \uc2 Tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) fell 0.4% to end at PEN11.60.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of 3.1575 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1570 to PEN3.1580.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1590 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1580 to PEN3.1600.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the session.   \par \par \uc2 In a report Friday,  \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  said that the sol is undervalued and that it will trade at PEN3.10 to the dollar in the near future.   \par \par \uc2 "In our view, given the degree of dollarization of the economy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate as a means to fight inflationary pressures (in addition to further monetary tightening)," it said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Katherine Gordon and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com -0- [ 08-03-07 1628ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070803e38300088\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
