\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Near Flat; Sol Ends Stronger   \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2007\par 22:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended near flat Friday as investors wait for more second quarter company results to be published.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the general index rose 9.15 points, or 0.04%, to end at 23,633.15.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index gained 0.59 points or 0.001% to end at 41,727.47.   \par \par \uc2 "The session was relatively quiet today. Investors seem to have taken a wait-and-see attitude," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 0.18% to end at 16.68 soles ($5.28). The share was heavily traded in the session.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) gained 1.94% to end at PEN138.64 on rising gold prices.   \par \par \uc2 In the other direction, copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) ended 1.54% lower at $29.50.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol Friday ended stronger at a midrate of 3.1575 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1570 to PEN3.1580.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1585 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1580 to PEN3.1590.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $77 million, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly this year to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The sol was also bolstered after the government Thursday placed sovereign bonds worth 4.75 billion soles, or some $1.5 billion, to raise cash for a prepayment to members of the Paris Club of nations.   \par \par \uc2 The 30-year sol-denominated bonds have a coupon of 6.9% and mature on Aug. 12, 2037.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 07-20-07 1656ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070720e37k000c4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
