\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Fall; Sol Ends Unchanged   \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2007\par 22:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes fell Wednesday on profit-taking.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the general index fell 116.89 points, or 0.49%, to end at 23,578.92. The selective blue-chip index ended 281.68 points, or 0.67%, lower at 41,584.53.   \par \par \uc2 "Fundamentally what we are seeing is profit-taking. Share prices have gone up as investors have been anticipating good second-quarter results. Those results are coming in and now they are taking profits," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Heavily traded zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 2.6% to 16.50 soles ($5.22). Earlier this week, Volcan reported second-quarter net income of $110.7 million, compared with $47.8 million in the same quarter a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc lead miner Compania Minera Atacocha SAA (ATACOI1.VL) fell 2.2% to PEN11.34. Atacocha on Wednesday reported second-quarter net income of $20.2 million, compared with $12.6 million in the same quarter a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended unchanged at a midrate of 3.1585 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1580 to PEN3.1590.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $40 million, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly this year to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 07-18-07 1645ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070718e37i00096\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
