\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End At New Record Highs   \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2007\par 22:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes jumped to new record highs on Friday, lifted again by optimism about second-quarter financial results.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the general index gained 323.44 points, or 1.39%, to end at 23,535.09.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 812.13 points, or 2%, higher at 41,498.57.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors have high expectations regarding the second-quarter results. That is what is making the market rise. In particular, they expect mining companies to show very positive balances," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 "There is also a great deal of excess liquidity in the market and investors are channeling this toward mining companies in particular," the trader added.   \par \par \uc2 He said the political noise of the past few days - tied to a strike by teachers - has had no impact on the market.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors consider it to be something isolated with very little political repercussions. If it continues, however, it could affect the market," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday, tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) gained 2.4% to end at 10.70 soles ($3.39) on a rise in tin prices.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rose 2.1% to $110.50, due to strength in copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) also gained, rising 3.3% to end at $28.10.   \par \par \uc2 Blue chip financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) rose 0.3% to end at $64.20.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended unchanged at a midrate of PEN3.1595 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1590 to PEN3.1600.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $103 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly this year to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Market analysts say there has been strong demand in the last few trading sessions for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tied in part to corporate tax payments and to pay special worker bonuses.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 07-13-07 1645ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070713e37d0007z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
