\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2007\par 23:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Wednesday when investors were encouraged by higher base metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the general index gained 82.29 points, or 0.36%, to end at 22,927.77.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 138.37 points, or 0.35%, higher at 40,171.74. "Rising metals prices helped push the indexes slightly higher today," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) gained 1.3% to end at 16.75 soles ($5.30) on stronger zinc prices.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) advanced 2.1% to $105.65, tracking higher copper prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 0.4% to $26.30.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors are also positive about second-quarter results that will be published soon," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of 3.1590 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1580 to PEN3.1600.   \par \par \uc2 The sol had ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1595 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1590 to PEN3.1600.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $152 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly this year to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said that there was strong demand Wednesday for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tied in part to corporate tax payment needs.   \par \par \uc2 Central Reserve Bank President Julio Velarde was quoted as saying Wednesday that last week's increase in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key reference rate to 4.75% from 4.5% won't have a large impact on the exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 "In principle it could have an impact on the exchange rate making interest rates on saving in soles more attractive, but that is being offset by an increase in interest rates on bonds in the United States," Velarde was quoted as saying by government news agency Andina.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 07-11-07 1706ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070711e37b00089\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
