\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2007\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended lower Tuesday, pulled down by lower metals prices that weakened mining companies shares.   \par \par \uc2 The two main indexes both fell back from Monday's record levels.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the general index declined 228.36 points, or 0.99%, to end at 22,845.48.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 442.73 points, or 1.09%, lower at 40,033.37.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) ended 2.1% lower at $26.20 on weaker copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) declined 0.5% to end at 16.53 soles ($5.23) as zinc prices eased.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) dropped 5.5% to end at PEN120.00.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) fell 2.6% to end at $61.05.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of 3.1595 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1590 to PEN3.1600.   \par \par \uc2 The sol had ended the previous session at a midrate of 3.1625 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1620 to PEN3.1630.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $93 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly this year to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said that there was strong demand Tuesday for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , likely tied to corporate tax payments and a special midyear worker bonus.   \par \par \uc2 Demand from outside of Peru for the sol was also noted, the analyst added.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 07-10-07 1634ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070710e37a000ae\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
