\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2007\par 22:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Thursday, as a number of mining companies gained on stronger metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, that index rose 173.96 points, or 0.78%, to end at 22,365.90.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 265.61 points, or 0.68%, higher at 39,314.13.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) increased 2.1% to end at $93.94 as copper prices increased.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) gained 0.6% to end at 16.35 soles ($5.16) on stronger zinc prices.   \par \par \uc2 Volcan has risen recently in part due to expectations that the company could post strong second quarter earnings, Banco de Credito said in report Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Tin miner  \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL) gained 0.5% to end at PEN10.40.   \par \par \uc2 Workers at Minsur's San Rafael mine and the company signed a new collective agreement earlier this week.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market will be closed Friday for a national holiday.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Thursday at a midrate of PEN3.1675 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1670 to PEN3.1680.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1695 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1690 to PEN3.1700.   \par \par \uc2 "For the coming week there could be some appreciation pressures on the sol, as a number of companies, especially exporters, demand the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make special bonus payments," Banco de Credito said.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $4.9 billion, which is estimated to be 14% higher than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases in all of 2006.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed Friday in observance of a national holiday.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak and Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 06-28-07 1653ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070628e36s000a0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
