\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Slightly Lower; Sol Stronger   \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2007\par 23:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended slightly weaker Wednesday when metals prices continued to slide.   \par \par \uc2 "The bulk of trade in Lima is always in mining companies and investors are very sensitive to price changes right now. They are less willing to take risks," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, that index fell 22.05 points, or 0.10%, to end at 22,191.94.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended down 56.49 points, or 0.14%, at 39,048.52.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) dropped 1.6% to end at $92 as copper prices declined.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 0.9% to end at 16.26 soles ($5.13).   \par \par \uc2 The market would have declined further but was helped by ongoing interest in shares linked to domestic demand, the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors are focused on shares linked to domestic demand, in particular companies that will benefit from a free trade agreement with the United States. There is a lot of optimism about the agreement right now," the trader added.   \par \par \uc2 The free trade deal between Peru and the U.S. was approved by the Peruvian Congress in June 2006, but still awaits approval by the U.S. Congress.   \par \par \uc2 Peru's Congress was on Wednesday considering a set of amendments tied to the free trade pact.   \par \par \uc2 Among others, agricultural producer Empresa Agroindustrial Pomalca SAA (POMALCC1.VL) gained 4.8% to PEN1.10.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended stronger Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.1695 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1690 to PEN3.1700.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1715 on a spread of PEN3.1710 to PEN3.1720.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday. So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $4.9 billion.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 06-27-07 1713ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070627e36r0009f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
