\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Close Higher; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2007\par 22:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Friday, rebounding from recent declines, as investors started to buy shares on the expectation of strong second-quarter corporate earnings.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index rose 43.97 points, or 0.20%, to end at 22,140.53.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 81.55 points higher, or 0.21%, at 38,994.56.   \par \par \uc2 "Basically what we saw today was a bit of a rebound after the corrections in recent sessions. The shares that fared the best were the shares linked to the agrarian sector and domestic demand," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors are beginning to take positions in shares in companies where they expect positive second-quarter results, in particular those linked to domestic demand," the trader added.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) increased 1.1% to end at 16.00 soles ($5.05).   \par \par \uc2 Beverage producer Union de Cervecerias Peruanas Backus & Johnston SAA (BACKUSI.VL) gained 3.5% to end at PEN3.00.   \par \par \uc2 Going the other way was financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP), which fell 3.2% to end at $60.00.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly weaker Friday at a midrate of PEN3.1695 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1690 to PEN3.1700.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1685 on a spread of PEN3.1680 to PEN3.1690.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Consulting company Macroconsult said in a report Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $4.9 billion so far this year in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , $957.9 million more than the net purchases in full year 2006.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak and Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 06-22-07 1643ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070622e36m0009h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
