\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Slightly Lower; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2007\par 22:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended slightly lower Thursday as some key base metals mining companies lost ground.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 57.30 points, or 0.26%, to end at 22,096.56.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 33.42 points, or 0.09%, lower at 38,913.01.   \par \par \uc2 Tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) declined 1.4% to end at 10.50 soles ($3.31) on weaker tin prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) lost 0.6% to $26.35 as copper prices eased.   \par \par \uc2 Moving in the other direction was precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN), which gained 1.9% to end at PEN114.75.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) rose 1.5% to $62.00.   \par \par \uc2 Banco de Credito said in a report Thursday that investors are starting to look forward to the release of second-quarter corporate financial results.   \par \par \uc2 "These speculative factors could add to volatility in coming days," it said   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly weaker Thursday at a midrate of 3.1685 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1680 to PEN3.1690.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of 3.1675 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1670 to PEN3.1680.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Upward pressure on the sol has weakened over the past two weeks or so, leading to fewer \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to analysts.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 06-21-07 1640ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070621e36l000by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
