\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Slightly Lower; Sol Unchanged   \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2007\par 22:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended slightly weaker Wednesday, following other weak regional stock markets.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 36.16 points, or 0.16%, to end at 22,153.86.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 103.98 points, or 0.27%, lower at 38,946.43.   \par \par \uc2 In the mining sector, copper miner  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) lost 1.5% to end at $93.41, while zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) declined 1.6% to end at 15.75 soles ($4.97).   \par \par \uc2 Going the other way was financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2 , (BAP) which rose 0.1% to end at $61.10.   \par \par \uc2 Credicorp runs Banco de Credito, Peru's largest bank.   \par \par \uc2 The Peruvian Banking Association said this week that Peru's past-due bank loan ratio fell to 1.62% in May, the lowest level on record.   \par \par \uc2 It added that Peru's total banking system loans rose to $17.77 billion, 27.3% higher than in the same month a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended unchanged Wednesday at a midrate of 3.1675 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1670 to PEN3.1680.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, purchasing $30 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 In a report Wednesday, Credit Suisse said that, "Dollar inflows into the country should remain strong for the rest of the year, and, thus, we expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem nominal appreciation pressures."   \par \par \uc2 It added that the government appears concerned about the consequences of losing competitiveness on account of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 06-20-07 1631ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070620e36k0009v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
