\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stk Indexes End Little Changed; Sol Strengthens A Bit   \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2007\par 22:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes were virtually unchanged Tuesday as investors continue to dabble in the market.   \par \par \uc2 "The market was stable, but still very cautious," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell two points, or 0.01%, to end at 22,190.02, while the selective blue-chip index rose 1.4 points, or 0.004%, to end at 39,050.41.   \par \par \uc2 The trader said that investor interest focused on Refineria la Pampilla SA (RELAPAC1.VL) and on construction company Grana y Montero. (GRAMONC1.VL). Relapsa shares gained 2.6% to 39.00 soles ($12.31), while Grana y Montero shares rose 1.36% to PEN7.45.   \par \par \uc2 "The price of the Pampilla shares is seen as attractive right now and Grana y Montero is attracting interest because different regions in Peru have more money for infrastructure projects," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 According to the latest figures from Peru's National Statistics Institute, construction output gained 13% in April on a strong rise in demand for cement from both the public and the private sectors for infrastructure projects.   \par \par \uc2 On the downside, copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) fell 0.64% to end at $26.40.   \par \par \uc2 "Copper prices were weaker but this was also profit-taking," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of 3.1675 soles to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1670 to PEN3.1680. The sol ended the previous session at a midrate PEN3.1680 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.1670 to PEN3.1690.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, purchasing $20 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221-7050 [ 19-06-07 2052GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070619e36j000y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
