\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's May 29 Foreign Reserves $21.30 Bln Vs $21.04 Bln   \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2007\par 14:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's net international reserves rose to $21.30 billion as of May 29, as the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to purchase U.S. dollars in open market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The latest total compares with $21.04 billion as of May 22, the Central Reserve Bank of Peru said late Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that the May 29 reserves were $1.60 million higher than at the end of April, due mainly to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which totaled $1.63 billion. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  position was $14.95 billion as of May 29, a rise of $1.37 billion from the end of April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  position doesn't include public sector deposits with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or commercial bank reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 04-06-07 1252GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070604e364000mw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
