\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End With Gains; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2007\par 22:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Monday, after posting an early decline, as investors continue to pour cash into commodity-producing companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index rose 180.39 points, or 0.87%, to end at 20,913.05.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 410.97 points, or 1.14%, higher at 36,359.92.   \par \par \uc2 Monday's gains follows a 3% advance by the general index Friday and an 8.55% surge Thursday. The general index fell 7.59% last Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "The indexes are recovering from the fall last week. Today, attention has focused on agriculture shares in particular," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 The general index is still down from a record high of 22,995.09 reached on May 9.   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) jumped 7.8% to end at $24.50 on stronger copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) rose 1.1% to $93.00.   \par \par \uc2 Agricultural products producer Empresa Agroindustrial Pomalca SAA (POMALCC1.VL) gained 7.9% to 0.96 sol ($0.30)   \par \par \uc2 In a report, brokerage Centura SAB said that share prices will likely benefit from positive sentiment as the release of second-quarter corporate financial results nears.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Monday at a midrate of PEN3.1695 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1690 to PEN3.1710.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1715 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1710 to PEN3.1720.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $55 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars regularly in recent sessions to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Scotiabank said in a report that it expects the sol to continue strengthening due in part to demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by companies that will have to pay taxes. Positive sentiment about Peru as a credit risk also will help boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it added.   \par \par \uc2 Peru's Finance Ministry, in macro-economic projections released late Friday, said that it expects the average exchange rate for this year to be PEN3.19 to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak and Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050 [ 06-04-07 1630ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070604e3640007n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
