\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Broad General Stock Index Ends 8.55% Higher   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2007\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's stock market ended sharply higher Thursday, rebounding from a precipitous drop the previous day, as investors flocked back into the market following Wednesday's shakeout.   \par \par \uc2 Contrary to the fevered selling on Wednesday, when the general index tumbled 7.6%, the Lima Stock Exchange's broad index ended 8.6% higher at 20,129.50 on Thursday. The selective blue-chip index ended 8.8% higher at 34,993.84.   \par \par \uc2 The general index's 168% gain in 2006 and double digit gains so far this year have sparked a stock market boom in the Andean nation. That has helped draw in many first-time individual investors, who have also poured money into mutual funds.   \par \par \uc2 Many of those individual investors, however, seem to be easily spooked.   \par \par \uc2 "In the last few months there was large inflow of investors who didn't have a clear idea what it meant to invest in the stock market. I think that a lot of investors who were speculating have now left," said Gonzalo Camargo, director of mutual fund company Fondos Continental, on CPN radio.   \par \par \uc2 The main stock indexes fell Wednesday mainly due to weakness in mining company shares and to a lesser extent by an earlier slide in the Chinese stock index. Some 60% of the general index is made up of mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 Officials worked late Wednesday and early Thursday to calm investors, pointing to the strength of the Peruvian economy.   \par \par \uc2 "This is purely psychological and speculative. No one could think this is an economic problem that could affect growth or inflation," President Alan Garcia said at a press conference early Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 He pointed out that growth in gross domestic product is expected to expand between 7% to 8% this year.   \par \par \uc2 "The fundamentals of the economy and the companies that trade on the bourse are very strong," stock market president Carmela de Marrou said in one media interview.   \par \par \uc2 "The market will have its ups and downs as it responds to supply and demand," she added.   \par \par \uc2 Among the gainers Thursday was copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA, (CVERDEC1.VL) up 10.2% to $21.80.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) ended 3.7% higher at $58.45.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) gained 2.0% to end at 102.00 soles. ($32.13)   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) rose 3.1% to end at $89.10.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended unchanged at a midrate of PEN3.1750 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1740 to PEN3.1760.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $36.5 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 So far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $4.53 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; \b \highlight22\uc2 peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 @dowjones.com; 51-1-221-7050 [ 05-31-07 1643ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070531e35v00092\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley10