\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Tumble Lower; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2007\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes tumbled lower Tuesday, as widespread selling continued on the Lima Stock Exchange.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 674.81 points, or 3.25%, to end at 20,066.77.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 1,455.98 points, or 4.01%, lower at 34,845.04.   \par \par \uc2 The general index is now down sharply from a record high of 22,995.09 reached May 9.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market had been boosted in good part by strong inflows of cash into mutual funds, and by individual investors investing directly.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say some of those investors may now be getting cold feet.   \par \par \uc2 "The last ones who came into the market may have been thinking of only short-term investments," said one market analyst, referring to the selling in recent sessions.   \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday,  \uc2 Peru Copper Inc.\uc2  (CUP) ended 14.9% lower at $5.15, following news that talks with an unnamed company had run out without any agreement on a merger or sale of the Toromocho copper project in central Peru.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) also fell, dropping 8.4% at end at $22.00.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) declined 1.1% to end at $58.33.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly weaker at a midrate of PEN3.1750 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1740 to PEN3.1760.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1735 soles to U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1730 to PEN3.1740.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $18 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves. -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050 -0- [ 05-29-07 1632ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070529e35t0008x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
