\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Mixed; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2007\par 23:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended mixed Friday when profit-taking continued.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 79.93 points, or 0.37%, to end at 21,248.31.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 218.74 points, or 0.59%, higher at 37,348.06.   \par \par \uc2 "What we are seeing is profit-taking with shares after the strong rally in the Peruvian market over the past few months," said one market analyst.   \par \par \uc2 In particular he pointed to zinc miner  \uc2 Compania Minera Volcan SA\uc2  (VOLCABC1.VL) that lost 0.25% to end at 15.96 soles ($5.03).   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) lost 0.8% to $25.50.   \par \par \uc2 "However, we are now seeing shares at attractive prices and there could be some bargain hunting in the next few sessions," the analyst added.   \par \par \uc2 In the other direction, one of the biggest gainers in Friday's market was  \uc2 Peru Copper Inc.\uc2  (CUP).   \par \par \uc2 The share gained 10.7% to $6.42 in a heavy trade on news that the company is negotiating with a third party that may buy the company.   \par \par \uc2 Peru Copper is developing the Toromocho copper project in the central Andes, which is now estimated to have 22 billion pounds of contained copper and over 840 million pounds of molybdenum.   \par \par \uc2 "It is definitely an interesting project but it requires a lot of financing," said the analyst.   \par \par \uc2 The sol, meanwhile, ended slightly weaker Friday at a midrate of PEN3.1710 soles to U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1700 to PEN3.1720.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1700 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1690 to PEN3.1710.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $120 million, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 So far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $4.45 billion.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    \par -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 05-25-07 1731ET ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070525e35p00081\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
