\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Peru Stk Indexes Tumble, Tracking Metals Prices; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2007\par 23:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, May 24, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 Peru's main stock indexes took a tumble Thursday, tracking a fall in metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 428.94 points, or 1.97%, to end at 21,328.24.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 748.69 points, or 1.98%, lower at 37,129.32.   \par \par \uc2 "Basically what we are seeing is a market that is reacting to the metals prices," one market analyst said. "As soon as they start falling, investors sell.   \par \par \uc2 "There is also some fear that the strong rise we saw in the first few months of the year has slowed, and some investors are opting to take profits now rather than later," he added.   \par \par \uc2 So far this year, the broad general index has gained around 70%.   \par \par \uc2 In Thursday's session, zinc miner  \uc2 Compania Minera Volcan SA\uc2  (VOLCABC1.VL)lost 2.4% to end at 16.00 soles ($5.05) on a fall in zinc prices.   \par \par \uc2 Among red metal miners,  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2  (PCU) dropped 2.3% to $84.60 when copper prices slid.   \par \par \uc2 Peru Copper Inc.\uc2  (CUP) also lost ground Thursday after rising strongly earlier in the week. The company's shares fell 1.7% to end at $5.80.   \par \par \uc2 According to traders, Peru Copper's shares had risen on rumors that the company is close to obtaining financing for the Toromocho copper project in central Peru.   \par \par \uc2 The sol, meanwhile, ended slightly weaker Thursday at a midrate of PEN3.1700 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1690 to PEN3.1710.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of 3.1665 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1660 to PEN3.1670.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $50 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221-7050   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 05-24-07 1705ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070524e35o005j0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
