\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Gain; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2007\par 23:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Wednesday when several blue-chip shares attracted investor interest after the slide in the previous session.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index gained 197.68 points, or 0.92%, to end at 21,757.18.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index rose 476.4 points, or 1.27%, to end at 37,878.01.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors felt the prices of several shares, in particular mining shares, were attractive and they opted to take advantage of them," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 He added, however, that the stock market "is volatile right now. Investors are more cautious than they were several weeks ago when the indexes kept hitting records."   \par \par \uc2 Copper miners, in particular, fared well in Wednesday's session.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner  \uc2 Peru Copper Inc.\uc2  (CUP) gained 7.3% to $5.90 in a heavy trade.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 2.5% to $26.90.   \par \par \uc2 A rise in gold prices helped boost precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN), which rose 4.2% to end at PEN105.50.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended weaker Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.1665 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1660 to PEN3.1670.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1655 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1650 to PEN3.1660.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $45 million.   \