\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Fall; Sol Ends Unchanged   \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2007\par 23:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes fell Tuesday when base metals prices took at downturn.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index lost 516.62 points, or 2.34%, to end at 21,559.50.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 809.63 points, or 2.12%, lower at 37,401.61.   \par \par \uc2 "Investors are paying close attention to metals prices right now. The prices started to fall and people started to sell," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 More than 60% of trading in the Lima stock exchange is in mining shares.   \par \par \uc2 Moreover, according to the trader, investors are also a bit more cautious now that the indexes have stopped consistently hitting record highs.   \par \par \uc2 "There is a sense that some shares have hit a maximum and there is some profit-taking," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc lead miner Compania Minera Atacocha SAA (ATACOI1.VL) declined 0.4% to 10.55 soles ($3.33) while zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) fell 2.4% to PEN16.59.   \par \par \uc2 Base metals miner  \uc2 Compania Minera Milpo\uc2  SAA (MILPOC1.VL) fell 3.7% to PEN18.30.   \par \par \uc2 Brokerage Centura SAB late Monday issued a "sell" recommendation Milpo and Atacocha and a "hold" recommendation for Volcan.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended unchanged Tuesday at a midrate of PEN3.1655 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1650 to PEN3.1660.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $75 million, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 05-22-07 1700ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070522e35m0008f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
