\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Post Another Decline; Sol Stronger   \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2007\par 22:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended lower Thursday, mainly due to weakness in a few key mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 82.75 points, or 0.38%, to end at 21,473.47.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 275.58 points, or 0.74%, lower at 37,118.85.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market's general index has now fallen every day since May 9, when it hit a record high 22,995.09 points.   \par \par \uc2 "There have been some declines after the market overheated when there was strong demand for shares," said one market analyst. "I think that the euphoria has become more reasonable."   \par \par \uc2 Weaker copper prices helped dragged down copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL), which lost 2.4% to end at $26.10.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 0.6% to end at 16.40 soles ($5.19) in heavy trading.   \par \par \uc2 Going the other way was  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 , (PCU) which gained 0.1% to end at $85.60.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) also gained, rising 1.6% to end at PEN103.50.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Thursday at a midrate of PEN3.1610 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1600 to PEN3.1620.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1640 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1630 to PEN3.1650.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $185 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said that demand for soles has remained strong, especially from foreign investors.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 05-17-07 1656ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070517e35h0008b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
