\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Weaker; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2007\par 22:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended weaker Tuesday, as a wide range of blue chip shares declined on profit-taking.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 131.46 points, or 0.59%, to end at 22,171.89.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 268.77 points, or 0.70%, lower at 38,324.82.   \par \par \uc2 "The indexes were stable, positive at the beginning of the session but toward the end investors began to sell shares. The fall was cushioned somewhat by the fact that metals prices remained steady," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 He also pointed to the entry of  \uc2 Panoro Minerals Ltd\uc2  (PML), a Canadian mineral exploration company. The company is the fourth Canadian junior mining company to list on the Lima Stock Exchange.   \par \par \uc2 "It did well for its first day trading," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 The share opened at $0.81 and rose to $0.96 before settling at $0.86 at the close in heavy trade.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) dropped 0.8% to end at $60.01.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) lost 5.9% to end at 102.10 soles ($32.31).   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) fell 0.6% to end at $86.50.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN3.1640 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1630 to PEN3.1650.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1665 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1660 to PEN3.1670.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $125 million.   \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said there was demand from foreign clients for soles during the session.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050 [ 05-15-07 1650ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070515e35f00093\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
