\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Sharply Lower; Sol Stronger   \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2007\par 23:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply lower Monday, dragged down mainly by weakness in metals prices that hurt mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 661.07 points, or 2.88%, to end at 22,303.35. The selective blue-chip index ended 1,365.66 points, or 3.42%, lower at 38,593.59.   \par \par \uc2 "The indexes were correcting for the entire session but took a stronger downturn right at the end on profit-taking. It moved fast," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 "The metals prices had a strong influence on the market today. Both the price of zinc and copper fell, and that had a big influence in the session," he said, pointing out that 60% of the trading on the Lima stock exchange is in mining shares.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) and Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) were among the miners that lost ground over the course of the session.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper dropped 4.4% from Friday's close to end at $86.57, while zinc miner Volcan lost 4.9% to end at 16.41 soles ($5.18).   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) also lost ground, retreating 2.1% to end at $60.50.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN3.1665 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1660 to PEN3.1670, the official said.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1705 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.17 to PEN3.1710.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday to purchase $5 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to buy dollars in recent sessions to smooth movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Scotiabank said in a report that it expects the sol to come under some moderate upward pressure due to tax payments.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050 [ 05-14-07 1710ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070514e35e0008e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
