\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Mixed; Sol Unchanged   \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2007\par 22:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended mixed Friday with some key blue chip shares gaining ground, but others important shares falling back.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 5.23 points, or 0.02%, to end at 22,964.42.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 44.96 points, or 0.11%, higher at 39,959.25.   \par \par \uc2 "The indexes were mixed and stable today with high volume. We expected them to correct more today but the news about the free-trade agreement (deal in the U.S.) and Credicorp results kept them from falling any further," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 According to the trader, investors were upbeat about a political deal in Washington, announced late Thursday, that could finally allow the Andean nation to obtain a trade deal with the U.S.   \par \par \uc2 Late Thursday,  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) announced first-quarter net income of $79.01 million, up from $51.19 million in the same quarter last year.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday, Credicorp, which owns Peru's largest bank, rose 4.2% to end at $61.80.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) continued to benefit from strong investor interest, gaining 1.4% to end at $90.56.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) went the other way, though, ending 0.5% lower at 108.50 soles. ($34.22)   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol Friday ended unchanged at a midrate of PEN3.1705 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1700 to PEN3.1710.   \par \par \uc2 Consulting company Macroconsult said in a report that the sol has been bolstered recently by flows of cash into Peru to invest in the stock market.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday to purchase $25 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050 -0- [ 05-11-07 1645ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070511e35b0007z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
