\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Mixed; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2007\par 22:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended mixed Thursday, with the broad general index posting a slight decline.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index fell 25.44 points, or 0.11%, to end at 22,969.65.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 113.02 points, or 0.24%, higher at 39,914.29.   \par \par \uc2 "The indexes ended mixed Thursday on profit-taking after strengthening early on," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 He said that the indexes were initially boosted by base metals miner  \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) after the announcement that it would list shares on the London Stock Exchange and on the Santiago Stock Exchange.   \par \par \uc2 Volcan ended 0.7% lower at 17.78 soles ($5.61).   \par \par \uc2 The indexes corrected toward the end of the session as "investors took profits due to the strong rises recently. In my opinion there will be a similar correction in tomorrow's session," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Several blue chip shares rose during the session.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) gained 1.5% to end at $89.33, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 0.7% to end at $28.70.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2  (BAP) ended 1.5% higher to end at $59.30. It owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly weaker, at a midrate of PEN3.1705 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1700 to PEN3.1710.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1665 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1660 to PEN3.1670.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $40 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050 [ 05-10-07 1646ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070510e35a000c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
