\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 2.23% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2007\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes continued on their relentless climb higher Wednesday, once again reaching new record highs.   \par \par \uc2 Mining companies again led the increases, but the gains were widespread on the Lima Stock Exchange.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the stock market's broad general index rose 501.12 points, or 2.23%, to end at 22,995.09.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 1,105.32 points, or 2.86%, higher at 39,801.27.   \par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of cash from mutual funds coming into the market," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 Not including Wednesday's gains, the general index has risen 75% so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 Base metals miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) again posted strong gains, ending 9.8% higher Wednesday at 17.90 soles ($5.66).   \par \par \uc2 Volcan said Wednesday that it will list its "A" and "B" shares on the London Stock Exchange and on the Santiago Stock Exchange.   \par \par \uc2 The company currently trades on the Lima Stock Exchange and on Latibex, the Spanish stock exchange for Latin American companies.   \par \par \uc2 Other miners also gained, with  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rising 2.1% to end at $87.80, and precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) increasing 0.9% to end at PEN110.00.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2  (BAP) ended 0.1% higher to end at $58.45. It owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol Wednesday ended slightly weaker, at a midrate of PEN3.1665 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1660 to PEN3.1670.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1655 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1650 to PEN3.1660.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $110 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that the sol has appreciated due to strong economic fundamentals, including strong exports.   \par \par \uc2 Flows of dollars into Peru from Peruvians overseas have also risen, while investors are also purchasing soles in order to invest in the stock market, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050   \par \par \uc2 [ 05-09-07 1640ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070509e3590008g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
