\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 2.53% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2007\par 22:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes soared to new record highs Friday, as strength in mining company shares drove the market upward.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index gained 530.51 points, or 2.53%, to end at 21,476.45.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 995.74 points, or 2.78%, higher at 36,784.20.   \par \par \uc2 "The stock market has reached a new record by rising over 21,000 points, due to a group of mining shares that are gaining on solid financial results and rising metals prices, especially copper and zinc," said Edgar Zavaria, with brokerage Latinoamericana SAB.   \par \par \uc2 "The stock market can keep rising, especially the miners, although it will likely be with a few days rising and then a correction, like a saw blade, although the trend is definitely upwards," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rose 2.3% to end at $83.40 on stronger copper prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 2.3% at end at $27.10.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) gained 1.9% to end at 107.00 soles ($33.75) as gold prices gained.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) also continued to rise, ending 0.7% higher to end at $56.00.   \par \par \uc2 Its main holding, Banco de Credito, (BDC.VL) reported net income of 236 million soles ($74 million) in the first quarter, compared with PEN154.7 million in the same period a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Friday at a midrate of PEN3.1645 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1640 to PEN3.1650.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1690 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1680 to PEN3.1700.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase a record $250 million.   \par \par \uc2 That was the largest single day purchase ever on the part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.   \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said that a Peruvian company had made a large sale of U.S. dollars, which had caused appreciation pressures on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Peru's sol is expected to gradually trade towards a PEN3.15 to the U.S. dollar target, Deutsche Bank said in a report Friday.   \par \par \uc2 It said the appreciation will come about despite ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars, due to strong fundamentals and a "supportive" technical position, as banks hold large net U.S. dollar positions.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050 [ 05-04-07 1624ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070504e3540009u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
