\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 1.19% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2007\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended at new record highs Thursday, boosted mainly by strength in mining company shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index gained 246.02 points, or 1.19%, to end at 20,945.94.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 705.38 points, or 2.02%, higher at 35,788.46.   \par \par \uc2 "What is lifting the stock market is good liquidity and the medium and long term buying by people betting that Peru will sign a free trade deal with the United States and receive an investment grade rating," said Hernando Pastor, a trader with brokerage Juan Magot & Asociados.   \par \par \uc2 "I think that the trend is positive due to liquidity from mutual funds and the good prices for metals, despite fluctuations," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miners fared well Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rose 1.0% to end at $81.50 on stronger copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 1.9% at end at $26.49.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) increased 1.8% to end at PEN14.50.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2  (BAP) also continued to rise, ending 2.0% higher to end at $55.60.   \par \par \uc2 Its main holding, Banco de Credito (BDC.VL), reported net income of 236 million soles ($74 million) in the first quarter, compared with PEN154.7 million in the same period a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Thursday at a midrate of PEN3.1690 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1680 to PEN3.1700.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1715 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1710 to PEN3.1720.   \par \par \uc2 Appreciation pressures on the sol have remained constant due to demand for investments purposes, and from companies betting that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will appreciate, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $65 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050 [ 05-03-07 1638ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070503e35300084\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
