\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes Rise On Blue Chips,Miners; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2007\par 22:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Wednesday, lifted again by strength in various blue chip shares and by gains in the shares of some mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index gained 25.14 points, or 0.12%, to end at 20,699.92.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index ended 97.46 points, or 0.28%, higher at 35,081.11.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market was closed Tuesday for the Labor Day holiday.   \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) rose 4.0% to end at $54.50.   \par \par \uc2 Its main holding, Banco de Credito (BDC.VL), reported net income of 236 million soles ($74 million) in the first quarter, compared with PEN154.7 million in the same period a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Various miners also gained.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) jumped 2.9% to end at PEN105.00.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) increased 6.0% to end at PEN14.10, while tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) moved 4.5% higher to end at PEN11.00.   \par \par \uc2 "In the case of Volcan and Minsur, it appears that some big funds have started to put money in them instead of in other mining companies," said a trader with brokerage Juan Magot SAB.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.1715 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1710 to PEN3.1720.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1725 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1720 to PEN3.1730.   \par \par \uc2 Appreciation pressures on the sol have remained constant due to demand for investments purposes, and from companies betting that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will appreciate, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $60 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was closed Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050 [ 05-02-07 1642ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070502e3520007p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
