\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Decline; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2007\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock index fell Monday, weighed down by weakness in some key blue chip shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index dropped 106.99 points, or 0.51%, to end at 20,674.78.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index declined, ending 352.19 points, or 1.0%, lower at 34,983.65.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market will be closed Tuesday for the May 1 holiday.   \par \par \uc2 Among those shares that declined Monday were several mining companies, which could have been affected to some degree by the national mining sector strike that started Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "The strike could have had some impact but nothing very strong since it was only partial and not all workers took part," said Eduardo Balbuena of brokerage Cartisa SAB.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) declined 0.5% to end at $82.13. Workers at two of its mines and a smelter and refinery complex in Peru have gone on strike to back various demands.   \par \par \uc2 Base metals miner  \uc2 Compania Minera Milpo\uc2  SAA (MILPOC1.VL) dropped 4.5% to end at 16.59 soles ($5.23) after the company lost out in a government auction for a large copper deposit.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2  (BAP) lost 0.2% to end at $52.40.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly weaker Monday at a midrate of PEN3.1725 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1720 to PEN3.1730.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1710 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1700 to PEN3.1720.   \par \par \uc2 Consulting company Macroconsult said in a report that demand for the sol has remained strong from foreigners who want to invest in the Andean nation and from banks and companies who are betting that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will appreciate.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $70 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will also be closed Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 04-30-07 1634ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070430e34u0007w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
