\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 0.43% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2007\par 22:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock index rose to a new record high Friday, lifted mainly by mining companies that rose on higher metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 89.74 points, or 0.43%, to end at 20,781.77.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index declined, however, ending 19.07 points, or 0.05%, lower at 35,335.84.   \par \par \uc2 "Right now the market is being moved by good first quarter earnings reports," a trader said Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) gained 0.8% to end at $82.50.   \par \par \uc2 Late Thursday copper miner Southern Copper said its first quarter net income totaled $563.5 million, up from $421.6 million in the same quarter a year earlier, as net sales rose.   \par \par \uc2 Base metals miner  \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLB.VL) continued to be heavily traded, ending 1.3% higher at 13.80 soles. ($4.35) The miner recently posted strong first quarter financial results.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2  (BAP) gained 0.2% to end at $52.50.   \par \par \uc2 Credicorp should post solid first quarter earnings as it continues to benefit from the strong economy and good loan growth, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol continued to strengthen, ending slightly stronger Friday at a midrate of PEN3.1710 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1700 to PEN3.1720.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1735 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1730 to PEN3.1740.   \par \par \uc2 Demand for soles is coming from investments in sol-denominated instruments, banks buying soles to cover the sales of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges, and corporate purchases of soles for taxation and salary payments, especially by mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $80 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 So far this week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $420 million.   \par \par \uc2 So far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $2.79 billion, helping lift Peru's net international reserves to a new record high of $19.39 billion as of April 24.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-27-07 1636ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070427e34r0008l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
