\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Weaken Slightly; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2007\par 22:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes declined slightly Thursday, pulled down by weakness in the mining sector but lifted by good financial results for other smaller companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index fell 11.35 points, or 0.05%, to end at 20,692.03.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index decreased 51.52 points, or 0.15%, to finish at 35,354.91.   \par \par \uc2 "The indexes would have fallen further as they were being pulled down by sliding metals prices but several companies published their first quarter results, which were very good. That helped," a trader said.   \par \par \uc2 The biggest gainer in Thursday's market was soft drink and water producer Corporacion Jose R. Lindley SA, (CORJRLI1.VL) which posted strong first quarter results.   \par \par \uc2 The share gained 15.2% to 1.67 soles ($0.53).   \par \par \uc2 The trader also pointed to solid first quarter financial results posted by electricity company Edelnor SAA. (EDELNOC1.VL).   \par \par \uc2 That share gained 11.1% to PEN2.60.   \par \par \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 , (BAP) meanwhile, gained 0.4% to end at $52.50.   \par \par \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 , Peru's largest financial holding company, is expected to post solid first quarter earnings as it continues to benefit from the strong economy and good loan growth, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 Going the other way were several big mining companies, which fell on weakness in metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) lost 1.0% to end at PEN104.00.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) lost 1.3% to end at $81.90, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) dropped 1.1% to end at $26.85.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Thursday at a midrate of PEN3.1735 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1730 to PEN3.1740.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1745 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1740 to PEN3.1750.   \par \par \uc2 Banco de Credito noted in a report that demand for soles is coming from various directions, including investments in sol-denominated instruments, banks buying soles to cover the sales of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges, and corporate purchases of soles for taxation and salary payments, especially by mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday to purchase $90 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 So far this week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $340 million. So far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $2.71 billion.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-26-07 1652ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070426e34q0008c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
