\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Weaken On Metal Prices;Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2007\par 22:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes weakened Wednesday, as various mining companies gave up their recent gains.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index fell 48.75 points, or 0.23%, to end at 20,703.38.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index decreased 93.15 points, or 0.26%, to finish at 35,406.43.   \par \par \uc2 "Early in the session the indexes declined because metals prices fell. Midway through trading Volcan published its first-quarter results, which were very good and this helped the indexes recover somewhat," a trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 0.8% to end at 13.24 soles ($4.16).   \par \par \uc2 Sharply higher revenue helped lift its first-quarter net income to $94.9 million compared with $20.9 million in the same quarter a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Going the other way was copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA, (CVERDEC1.VL) which declined 0.6% to end at $27.15.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) lost 0.1% to end at PEN84.00.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended stronger Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.1745 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1740 to PEN3.1750, the official said.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1765 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1760 to PEN3.1770.   \par \par \uc2 The sol has also been gaining ground recently as companies seek the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for tax payment purposes, and due to increased investments.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $100 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-25-07 1638ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070425e34p0007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
