\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 0.11% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2007\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes rose Tuesday to new record highs, boosted again by mining company shares, although the gains were less robust than in recent trading sessions.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 22.48 points, or 0.11%, to end at 20,752.13.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 138.22 points, or 0.39%, to finish at 35,499.58.   \par \par \uc2 The increase in the mining sector came about despite weak metals prices, as investors continue to look forward to expected strength in first-quarter earnings for Peru's miners.   \par \par \uc2 "Today the market was not as dynamic. Metals prices fell and that lead to some profit taking although some companies fared quite well," one trader said, pointing to Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL).   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde increased 5.0% to end at $27.30, while tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) gained 1.3% to end at 10.85 soles ($3.41).   \par \par \uc2 Going the other way was copper miner  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 ,(PCU), which declined 0.08% to end at $82.93.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Tuesday at a midrate of PEN3.1765 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1760 to PEN3.1770, the official said.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1775 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1770 to PEN3.1780.   \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said demand for the sol was widespread Tuesday, coming from both local and foreign investors.   \par \par \uc2 The sol has also been gaining ground recently as companies seek the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for tax payment purposes.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $100 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 -0- [ 04-24-07 1633ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070424e34o00073\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
