\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Index Rises 0.35% To End At Record   \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2007\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes Monday rose to new record highs, as mining company gains again propelled the stock market.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results from the Lima Stock Exchange, the stock market's broad general index rose 72.97 points, or 0.35%, to end at 20,729.65.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 277.16 points, or 0.79%, to finish at 35,361.36.   \par \par \uc2 "Market sentiment was mixed today, on the one hand there was profit-taking because of strong rises in recent sessions, but the declines was compensated for by interest in some mining shares," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner  \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLB.VL) gained 1.9% to end at 13.14 soles ($4.13) on improved zinc prices.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 4.0% to end at $26.00, while  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) rose 3.1% to end at $83.00, as copper prices gained.   \par \par \uc2 In a report, Scotiabank said that it expects volumes on the bolsa to continue to grow. It noted that daily volumes are now some $59 million, about double what they were earlier this year.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol ended slightly stronger Monday at a midrate of PEN3.1775 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1770 to PEN3.1780.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.1780 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN3.1770 to PEN3.1790.   \par \par \uc2 The sol has been gaining ground recently as companies seek the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for tax payment purposes.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $50 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent sessions to buy dollars to ease movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires;peru@dowjones.com; 51-1-221 7050 [ 04-23-07 1646ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020070423e34n0007f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
